FUTURE PLANS :

- full dirty-tracking / partial re-render (React-style reconciliation): would mean per-component
	change detection + keyed diffing + invalidation plumbed through every mutation path.

going into edit mode should make the entire wire network in edit mode, so every wire that the (clicked) wire is connected to

separate the rendering from logic (rn lagging logic laggs the ui too) :
	Don't block the UI at all.
	The lock-holding-worker-thread design means any nonzero sweep time is a freeze.
	Kicking the logic to a separate thread (or dropping/reacquiring the sim lock between chunks) would keep rendering responsive during difficult stuff regardless of how fast the logic itself runs.


add components or some form of input that can run rust code (like toggling a setting with your own circuits)

nicer documentation : in game features, keybinds, maybe some educational stuff like how to use x-y, or maybe to help make complex circuits (or atleast links to real help)
